@page "/components/dialog"

<PageTitle>Dialog — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Dialog</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> opened with <code>showModal()</code>, so the focus trap,
    the inert background, Escape and the top layer are the browser's. Radix's Portal and Overlay
    have no counterpart here, and that is a feature rather than a gap.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    When the content comes from the server, an Unpoly overlay is usually the better tool:
    <code>up-layer="new"</code> renders a real, bookmarkable route into a modal.
    <code>&lt;Dialog&gt;</code> is for content the page already has.
</p>

